69 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 55 0 R
/E (As the demand for patient-centered care and clinical pharmacy grew across Asia, so did the need for a platform to share knowledge. This vision began in 1996, when leaders from China, Korea, Japan, and the USA conceived a forum for practical exchange.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
70 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 55 0 R
/E (The journey started humbly in 1997 with the first conference \(originally EACDCPPE\) held in the USA, attended by just 36 representatives. By 1999, the second meeting in Shanghai highlighted the unique developmental needs of Asian pharmacy practice compared to the West.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
71 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 55 0 R
/E (A pivotal transformation occurred in 2003 in Japan, where the event was rebranded as the Asian Conference on Clinical Pharmacy \(ACCP\). This marked a new era of expansion, welcoming nations like the Philippines, Indonesia, and Singapore. Recognizing the explosive growth of the profession, members at the 2005 Malaysia conference voted to move from biennial to annual meetings, ensuring continuous collaboration for a sustainable future.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
endobj
72 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 55 0 R
/E (Now, we are honored to welcome the world back for a third time. In 2026, Thailand will host the 25th ACCP in the vibe rant city of Bangkok under the visionary theme: "Borderless Pharmacy Practice: The Collaboration for Sustainability and Cultural Integration.")
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
73 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 55 0 R
/E (We invite you to immerse yourself in the dynamic and diverse culture of Bangkok, a city where tradition meets modernity. Beyond the cultural experience,             this conference is a vital platform to:)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
endobj
